-1a1520e150f7" :question/id #uuid "0f86b247-8f09-549d-8811-1a1520e150f7" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $Q$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $Q$ is a singular matrix\n- **II.** $Q$ is **not** a singular matrix\n- **III.** $det(Q)=0$\n\n$$\nQ=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4 \\sqrt{2}}{3} & -1 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{2 \\sqrt{2}}{3} & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ - \\frac{8 \\sqrt{2}}{3} & 2 & - \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4 \\sqrt{2}}{3} & -1 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{2 \\sqrt{2}}{3} & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ - \\frac{8 \\sqrt{2}}{3} & 2 & - \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{4 \\sqrt{2}}{3}|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ 2 & - \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2 \\sqrt{2}}{3} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ - \\frac{8 \\sqrt{2}}{3} & - \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}|+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2 \\sqrt{2}}{3} & \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ - \\frac{8 \\sqrt{2}}{3} & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{4 \\sqrt{2}}{3}(- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2}- \\sqrt{2})+1(- \\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{8}{3})+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(\\frac{4 \\sqrt{2}}{3}+4 \\sqrt{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4 \\sqrt{2}}{3}\\cdot (- \\frac{5 \\sqrt{2}}{2})+1\\cdot \\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{16 \\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\  & =- \\frac{20}{3}+\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{16}{3} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(Q)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["885ed53f-bd5b-5462-9002-72b92ffeea39" "6c836807-d3ab-5654-828e-8cfc6899a48e" "7319f1b7-7a37-509